       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Dose ordered:** 4250 mg three times daily is 12,750 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day (about 850 mg three times daily). The maximum for extended-release is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** This is about five times the maximum. It carries a serious risk of metformin-associated lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg** by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- **425 mg** by mouth three times daily with meals\n- **1,000 mg** by mouth twice daily with meals\n\nIf 4250 mg is what you want, tell me and add a note on the clinical rationale. I'll enter it as written. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
